(1c) CORRECTED: is distinct kill-sets <= |{+-v mod q}| (the safe direction)?
    150 pairs: violations of distinct <= pmclasses = 0; strictly fewer = 53
    => the pairing lemma direction holds; the converse fails, so pmclasses is a
       CONSERVATIVE proxy (real blocking capacity is often lower still).

(3c) TARGETED ATTACK, corrected: speeds in a fixed class r mod m
     (differences become multiples of m -- highly composite, low phi/k)
     188 primitive fixed-class families tested
     lowest certificate margin: 1
       V = [1, 211, 421, 631, 841, 1051]... (first 6)
       best beat = (2, 'sieve', 1)

(4c) WHY THIS CONSTRUCTION CANNOT BE PUSHED FURTHER
     To make DIFFERENCES highly composite, put all speeds in one class mod m.
     Then sums are 2r + multiples of m.  To make SUMS composite too you need
     2r = 0 mod m, i.e. r = 0 or m/2 -- and both force gcd(V) > 1, i.e. a
     NON-PRIMITIVE family, which dilation invariance (THM-1050) reduces away.
       m= 210 r=   0: gcd(V) =  210  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
       m= 210 r= 105: gcd(V) =  105  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
       m= 120 r=   0: gcd(V) =  120  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
       m= 120 r=  60: gcd(V) =   60  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
       m=  60 r=   0: gcd(V) =   60  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
       m=  60 r=  30: gcd(V) =   30  non-primitive -> dilation reduces it
